{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CghcTPeKzxc1er5kd8VTz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Setup:** The crossover occurs where the high-spin ⁵T₂g(t₂g⁴e_g²) and low-spin ¹A₁g(t₂g⁶) energies are equal.\n\n**Energies** (Racah parameters A, B, C; Dq is the octahedral crystal-field parameter):\n\n- ⁵T₂g has energy 15A − 21B − 4Dq. The free-ion ⁵D term has no C dependence.\n- ¹A₁g is the closed t₂g⁶ shell, so its energy is the sum of the electron-pair repulsions plus −24Dq. I used the standard Racah integrals for t₂g orbitals, quoted from memory:\n  - same orbital: J = A + 4B + 3C\n  - different orbitals: J = A − 2B + C\n  - exchange: K = 3B + C\n- The pair count is 3 same-orbital pairs, 12 different-orbital J terms and 6 exchange terms. This gives a repulsion of 3J_ii + 12J_ij − 6K_ij = 15A − 30B + 15C.\n- So E(¹A₁g) = 15A − 30B + 15C − 24Dq.\n\n**Crossover condition:**\n\nE(¹A₁g) − E(⁵T₂g) = −9B + 15C − 20Dq = 0\n\nSo Dq = (15C − 9B)/20.\n\n**Numbers:**\n\n- 15C = 15 × 3078 = 46 170 cm⁻¹\n- 9B = 9 × 803 = 7 227 cm⁻¹\n- Dq = (46 170 − 7 227)/20 = 38 943/20 ≈ 1947 cm⁻¹, so 10Dq ≈ 19 470 cm⁻¹.\n\nDq/B ≈ 2.4 and C/B ≈ 3.8 here. I didn't check this against a Tanabe–Sugano diagram.\n\nFor Dq below about 1947 cm⁻¹ the ground state is high-spin ⁵T₂g. For Dq above that it is low-spin ¹A₁g.\n\n{\"Dq\": 1947, \"B\": 803, \"C\": 3078, \"out_of_scope\": false, \"reason\": \"Crossover where E(1A1g)=E(5T2g) gives Dq=(15C-9B)/20.\"}"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":775,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":775,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"de78bd46-61fe-4e3a-89be-5e6395900180